# Static look-alike mushroom (#299), native 24x16, one frame: the same cap-and-stem tuft family as the honey fungus pair (D63), so a
# first meeting makes the player wary, but muted caps with paler speckles, a visible ring on every stem (like the harmless
# honey fungus, the opposite of the ringless lethal false honey fungus), no golden glow, no honey brown, no lime. It never animates.
# Decor tier (D76, #344, 2026-11-16): recoloured to muted grey-beige with a contour in its own hue, no ink 0b0814, so it reads as
# scenery; the tuft shape and the rings stay. The real-or-false game stays between the two active fungi (D63).
# Night palette (D92, #430): every colour mixed 35 % toward the night background 2c3f66; the day values are in docs/ART_DIRECTION.md.
# Layered-forest recolour (#236, D112): OKLab L x0.55 - 0.10, hue kept, over forest-2's near-black ground: outline 0.157, body 0.145.
